a)	Create a new Spring Boot project.
Aim: To bootstrap a structured Spring Boot application using Spring Initializr configured with database connectivity and persistence dependencies. 

Procedure:
1.	Navigate to the online initialization interface at [https://start.spring.io/](https://start.spring.io/). 
2.	Set up the project configuration variables: 
o	Project: Maven Project 
o	Language: Java 
o	Spring Boot: Latest Stable Version 
3.	Click Add Dependencies and select the following operational modules: 
o	Spring Web
o	Spring Data JPA (Java Persistence API bundle) 
o	H2 Database (In-memory structural relational SQL runtime engine) 
4.	Select Generate to export and download the complete repository zip archive file. 
5.	Unpack the compressed project files and import the root path into your IDE (VS Code / IntelliJ). 

b)	Add Spring Data JPA dependency.
Aim: To verify and explicitly define structural persistence and database driver capabilities within the core build orchestration document. 

Dependencies Configuration (pom.xml):
<dependencies>
    <!-- Core Spring Boot Web Starter Layer -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- Spring Data JPA Starter Layer for Object-Relational Mapping -->
    <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
    </dependency>

    <!-- H2 Relational Database Engine Runtime Scope -->
